From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:46:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: built-in 1ma plugins take over verified installed copies

Before patch 0014 the 1ma plugins were installed from 1ma's repository (git)
or from the Linux release folder (path). When a built-in 1ma plugin meets a
copy with its id, reconcileBundled now moves that row to the built-in source
instead of skipping it, keeping the enablement and, through the plugin id,
the settings, secrets, schedules and data. Only a verifiable 1ma source
qualifies: git from github.com/1ma-ai/1ma (compared by host and path) with
subdirectory plugins/<name>, or a folder carrying the release script's
.1ma-release.json; a copy newer than the built-in is kept. Every other copy
stays and the log says why.

An app from before 0014 deletes these rows, with their settings, at start;
bb's artifact GC removes a git checkout once no row points at it; and the
Linux release folder moves on. So before the first built-in 1ma row is
written, on a takeover or a clean install, <data>/backups/before-1ma-builtins/
is saved once and never replaced: the state of all four ids (installed, with
the plugin and artifact rows and a hashed copy of the checkout or release
folder, or absent) and a copy of the whole database. A copy is taken over only
when its install is in that state; without a usable state, and once the move
has begun, copies stay.

server/dist/one-ma-rollback.js, run with 1ma stopped, holds bb-app's runtime
claim on the data folder (so it refuses while 1ma runs), checks the saved
hashes and the rows before changing anything, then in one exclusive
transaction puts back the saved rows and file trees (a release folder's copy
goes to <data>/plugins/1ma-rollback/<id>) and removes the rows of 1ma plugins
that were not installed before, keeping their settings and data. It refuses
and names the database copy if an older version has run already, and renames
the set afterwards, so a later move saves the state of that time.
